<p>A senior Pakistani delegation led by Field Marshal Asim Munir arrived in Tehran on April 15 to keep diplomacy moving between Iran and the United States after weekend talks in Islamabad ended without a breakthrough. Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi welcomed the delegation, and Pakistani officials said the visit was part of a wider mediation effort to de-escalate nearly seven weeks of war and set up a second round of negotiations before a cease-fire expires. The push comes as Washington publicly denies reports that it sought a cease-fire extension, while saying talks about another round are still active and that Pakistan has become the main intermediary. At the same time, the conflict is spilling into vital shipping lanes: Iran has threatened key regional routes including the Red Sea, and pressure on maritime traffic is raising the stakes for any diplomatic opening.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/QbD92NYmaXlEJX4iBr5D7cfUIRAobdZeMqawaOGd607EiFhSw8rvsaKhL2atCJd6DRHnVyAPy-i5Q_g5DWEPUqC3lYN9b9ACO2FcSUKsY7I9' alt='This handout photo taken and provided by the Iranian Foreign Ministry on April 15, 2026 shows Iran’s Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi welcoming Chief of Defence Forces and Chief of Army Staff Field Marshal Asim Munir upon his arrival at the airport in Tehran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Messages exchanged: Baqaei said Pakistan had carried several messages since the Iranian delegation returned from Islamabad on Sunday, a sign that indirect talks continued even after the first round ended without agreement.</li><li>Possible venue: White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt said any new in-person talks would most likely take place in Pakistan again, though nothing had been finalized.</li><li>Shipping pressure: The Hindu reported that nine vessels turned back in 48 hours during Iran&#x27;s port blockade, showing how quickly the crisis is affecting commercial navigation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: Karoline Leavitt said reports that Washington sought a cease-fire extension were false and called Pakistan the &quot;only mediator&quot; as discussions on another round of talks continued. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/white-house-denies-us-requested-ceasefire-says-new-talks-may-happen-pakistan'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iran: Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi thanked Pakistan for its &quot;gracious hosting&quot; of the Islamabad dialogue and said the two countries shared a strong commitment to regional peace and stability. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991972/cdf-munir-visits-iran-alongside-delegation-as-part-of-mediation-efforts-holds-meeting-with-fm-araghchi'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistani coverage described the effort as a broader mediation push led by Munir alongside Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif, not just a one-off Tehran visit, after the Islamabad round stalled. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-war-news-pakistan-asim-munir-lands-in-iran-with-trumps-peace-offer-after-islamabad-talks-fail-11364237#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-pakistan-delegation-in-tehran-to-continue-talks/live-76802532'>Iran war: Pakistan delegation in Tehran to continue talks</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/15/world/iran-war-trump-us-israel'>Pakistani Mediators Arrive in Iran to Keep Peace Talks Alive</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/pakistani-mediators-arrive-in-iran-in-bid-to-keep-peace-talks-alive'>Pakistani mediators arrive in Iran in bid to keep peace talks alive</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3350225/iran-threatens-shut-down-red-sea-shipping-unless-us-lifts-naval-blockade'>US cites optimism over a deal even as Iran threatens to shut down Red Sea shipping</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-war-news-pa